---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy of NZSalary.com: What We Collect and Why" description="Privacy policy of NZSalary.com: calculations run in your browser, no personal data is sent, no account is needed, and what hosting logs and optional analytics involve." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Privacy', path: route('privacy', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang="en" />
    <h2>What happens to the numbers you type</h2>
    <p>Nothing leaves your device. Gross pay, tax code, KiwiSaver rate, student loan: the PAYE engine works them through in your browser, so they never reach us or anyone else, are saved on no server and cannot be connected to you. No account, newsletter or form exists to gather personal information. Once you edit a field, the address bar carries your values so the link can be shared; only the people who receive that link see them.</p>
    <h2>What the host sees</h2>
    <p>{LEGAL.hosting.name} serves the pages. Each request leaves a standard log entry (IP address, page, time, browser type) that the host keeps to run and protect the service. We make no use of those entries to identify anyone.</p>
    <h2>Statistics: Clarity and Google Analytics</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> (Microsoft Corporation) logs clicks, scroll depth, the pages viewed and their addresses, device, browser and a location estimated from the IP address, to build heatmaps and anonymous replays. Text typed into fields is masked before sending, but the values inside a shared link form part of the address it logs. Replays are kept 30 days and aggregates up to 13 months, possibly outside New Zealand, for instance in the United States (see the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft privacy statement</a>).</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (Google Ireland Limited) counts page views, referral sources, session length and engagement, device and browser, and a city-level location derived from an IP address it does not keep. Reports are held for 14 months. Data can go to Google LLC in the United States, certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework (see the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google privacy policy</a>).</li>
      <li>Both load with the first page, with no notice and no consent banner. To opt out, block third-party cookies or the clarity.ms and google-analytics.com domains, or install Google’s <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">opt-out add-on</a>; the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> lists each cookie. The calculators behave the same without them.</li>
      <li>No advertising script runs on NZSalary.com.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>The Privacy Act 2020 lets you ask any agency for access to, and correction of, personal information it holds about you; because the publisher is in France, the GDPR applies as well. We hold none from the calculators, but you can still write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. If the answer does not satisfy you, contact the Office of the Privacy Commissioner or France’s {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
